  <prompt>Owner UAT round 12, item O5. Record: `projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/042-uat-round12-2026-10-08.md`.</prompt>

  <goal>Outlook's Quick Save opens the same Spaarke progress -> result dialog as Word's (task 110) with an "Open in Spaarke" link to the saved .eml record; a suggestion the user cannot file to saves the email UNFILED and says so instead of refusing.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      - Word's controller `word/commands/quickSaveDialog.ts` and page `word/commands/notify.html` (task 110) are host-neutral except the page path; Outlook previously posted an item info bar and, for a non-fileable suggestion, did not save at all.
      - An unfiled save is a supported, required case (owner standing decision); the server accepts a save without `targetEntity`.
      - `GET …/communications/by-message-id/{id}/suggestions` 404 = "not saved yet"; `communicationSuggestionsService.fetchModel` already maps it to `null`.
    </background>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner O5">Reuse the Word controller and page (move the host-neutral parts to `shared/commands/`); Word behaviour unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner standing decision">No fileable suggestion (none, 404, or `canFile === false`) -> save unfiled, say so in the dialog ("Saved to Spaarke — not filed to a record. Open Spaarke to file it."); a fileable one is still filed. Never auto-file a guess.</constraint>
    <constraint source="no stale UI">No Outlook item info bar is left behind; the dialog is the only surface.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Tests: dialog opens before the save; success with link; unfileable -> unfiled + message; fileable -> filed; error path; event.completed once (via the dialog controller); 404 not logged as an error; Word tests unchanged in behaviour.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">The Outlook dialog opens before the prediction is read or the save posted, on `/outlook/commands-notify.html`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Success shows the record link built from ORG_URL + the job's artifact id; no link without ORG_URL.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`canFile === false`, no prediction, or a failed prediction posts a save without `targetEntity` and shows the unfiled message; `canFile` true/null/absent files to the suggestion with the friendly type name.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A failed job / failed POST / unreadable email show the error with no link; the command completes once through the dialog.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The build emits the notify page for both hosts; gates: jest green, lint 0, no production tsc errors, test-file TS errors not above 68.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step>Move controller + page to `shared/commands/`, add a `pagePath` dep; webpack emits the page for both hosts; shared `readSavedDocument`.</step>
    <step>Rewrite Outlook `quickSave` around the dialog; unfiled path (`buildEmailSaveRequest(…, null, …)`).</step>
    <step>Tests; gates; write `notes/118-outlook-quick-save-dialog.md`.</step>
  </steps>

  <justification>
    <existing>Task 110 controller/page; `buildQuickSaveRecordLink`; `readSavedDocument`.</existing>
    <extension>Yes — moved to shared and reused; no new component.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>UAT O5: Outlook Quick Save gave no pop-up, no link, and refused a save when the suggestion was a contact.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <relevant-files>
    <file role="edit">src/client/office-addins/outlook/commands/index.ts</file>
    <file role="move">src/client/office-addins/shared/commands/quickSaveDialog.ts</file>
    <file role="move">src/client/office-addins/shared/commands/notify.html</file>
    <file role="new">src/client/office-addins/shared/commands/readSavedDocument.ts</file>
    <file role="edit">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/services/quickSaveHelpers.ts</file>
    <file role="edit">src/client/office-addins/webpack.config.js</file>
  </relevant-files>
</task>
